A||||13||FieroLisa||Cleaning Products & exhaust||||1||
Z||000000||FieroLisa||07-16-2001||02:22 PM||||Couple of questions... I was at the Michigan show and realized that I'm running out of my cleaning products...so I was borrowing all sorts of crap. So I'm just wanting some opinions on your favorites for polish, upholstery, engine, dash (if anyone mentions armor all I'll kick your butt), etc etc.<P>Also my other question is about my exhaust. My muffler is CRAP. It's falling apart, and rattles everytime I accelerate. I just replaced the cat, which helped, but I know I need a new muffler. SO the question is, is it worth it to go with Flowmaster muffler, which is obviously cheaper than going with something like the entire Flowmaster exhaust system or Occelot from the Fiero Store.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT: 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air intake<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A>*<A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>NC Tarheels Fieros Site</A><P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.webjolt.f2s.com/pictures/fierolisa.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||bzzzted||07-16-2001||02:44 PM||||found that one of the better interior products is the spray on stuff, can't quite remember what its called?, black label, think it havs a viking type guy on it holding a shield.  Believe it even comes in a " wipe " package now! works real good on tires too!, think the manufacturer has some paint and wheel  cleaner also!... If anybody can help me remember what this is called??? <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><BR>||||reg||12
Z||000002||Formula88||07-16-2001||05:35 PM||||Hi Lisa!  I'm a guy and you're a girl!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Now that we've established that....<BR>For exhaust, I'd recommend the SpinTech muffler.  It's louder than stock, but not quite as loud as a Flowie.  It's also cheaper.  West Coast Fiero has them.  They're also working on a complete exhaust system, if you need any other piping.  I'm planning on their 2.5" exhaust with Hi-Flo cat and SpinTech for my Formula.<P>As for cleaning products, what do you use on the dash?  I'm tired of Armor All type products.  I don't want my interior looking like I coated it in vaseline. (unless of course, ... oh never mind  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">)  I do use Armor All on the tires, but that doesn't really count.<P>As for paint cleaning/polish, I'm using the McGuires 3 step system and really like it, but I'm gonna give Zaino a shot, cuz I've heard nothing but good stuff about it.  ||||reg||10
Z||000003||Jay||07-16-2001||07:01 PM||||Lisa I'm using McGuires 3 step also and I love it.  They also make an interior cleaner which doesn't leave that shiney cheap look that Armour Al...most said it leaves.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> As for the exhaust...can't help you I only got two catalytics and no muffler.  <P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR>1986 Northstar GT<BR>www.members.home.net/jaygrande<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/cayuga3_3.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Shaun41178||07-16-2001||08:21 PM||||I have a flowmaster for a camaro/firebird.  80 series I think it is.  I will sell it to you.<P>$40 plus $10 shipping.  Still new.  2.5 inch in and dual out<P>I think Jegs sells it for around $70 or so  LMK||||reg||1
Z||000005||Ditz88GT||07-16-2001||09:38 PM||||Will the Flowmaster for the camaro/firebird fit?  Just wondering, I had heard that the Grand-am Flowmaster was the one that fit...But I guess you wouldn't of listed it if it didn't fit.  So do both fit?<P>~Ditz88GT<BR> <A HREF="http://go.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://go.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||5
Z||000006||kslish||07-16-2001||11:25 PM||||Lisa, for your exhaust go for the most practical (and economical fix), a Spintech muffler in place of the stock one (I think the Spintech 311SC is the model that directly replaces the stock one but you may want to confirm that).  You can get them from West Coast Fiero or Spintech directly (www.spintechmufflers.com).  Should run you around $120 + shipping + installation.<P>I helped a friend install a Spintech on his recently purchased '88 GT t-top which had a stock exhaust, but the system was butchered by a previous owner....so we installed a Spintech with some custom bent stainless steel pipes (since everything from the cat back needed replaced).  We went with the Spintech because it seemed to be better constructed (it is one heck of a solidly built part) and was more of a direct fit than the Flowmaster.  The Spintech sound is nice (better than stock), but not quite as mellow as the Flowmasters I've heard on Fieros.  It's definately the exhaust I'd go with if I didn't have the 2 Borla catback systems sitting in my basement (no, you're not getting one of them)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Check out this thread for some more on the Spintech:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011543.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011543.html</A> <P>Don't go with the Ocelot....the rest of your exhaust is in pretty good shape, so no need to go replacing factory stainless steel pipes  with aluminized mild steel ones that will just end up rusting out eventually.  Plus you can have the Spintech purchased and installed for much less than even the initial purchase price of the Ocelot system.  <P>As for polishes, I'm a 3-step Meguire's man myself....you might want to ask Roger what he recommends.  Don't have any favorites for cleaning products for the interior and engine...usually whatever is cheap and on sale.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC<BR>See them at <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/kjslish/Fiero.html</A><BR>Western PA Fiero Club - <A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dave Gunsul||07-16-2001||11:56 PM||||I use a funny little product called Wenol<BR>for polishing alum.,chrome, and stainless.<BR>This stuff would polish a rock if you wanted to polish one!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>You can only get it from Summit Racing or Wenol themselves. <A HREF="http://www.summitracing.com" TARGET=_blank>www.summitracing.com</A> <BR>or 1-877-WENOL66<BR>Order the stuff in the red tube that's the stuff that works not the auto-Wenol.<P>As for wax: Super Glaze from the Wax Shop<BR>is the best stuff i've ever seen and blows<BR>all the other waxes that i've tryed away!<BR>You can usually get this from Pep Boys.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000008||Monkeyman||07-17-2001||05:13 AM||||Dave Gunsul--You can get Wenol lots of places.  I used to buy it all across the country when I was trucking.  Lots of the larger truckstops have it.  You are absolutely correct about how well it works.  Best stuff in the world (and probably the most expensive, but well worth it).<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000009||KRMFiero||07-17-2001||06:46 AM||||for my rims wheels i use:<BR>Prestone wheel cleaner<BR>Prestone whitewall/sidewall cleaner<P>after i use them i use regular dish soap and warm water to wash her then after it drys I...<BR>Use black majic on the sideways - spray it on then wipe it evenly (works better)<BR>for Wax I use Prestone wax, it comes with a free foam aplicator - I get the wax free though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000010||grinthock||07-17-2001||07:24 AM||||3 Step all the way on the outside, gives a nice Candy coat, lasts up to 3 months for me....||||reg||1
Z||000011||Dave Gunsul||07-17-2001||02:10 PM||||MM: that's very interesting to hear.<BR>It's also very nice to hear that someone<BR>knows what i'm talking about. Usually when I mention Wenol people just look at me funny.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I used to see Wenol in hardware stores too but in the last couple-a years the only place i've been able to find it anymore is<BR>Summit. I do see it at larger car show/swap meets sometimes and they do show up at the World of Wheels show here in IL but these are few and far between.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>As for the price: Summit sells it for $7.50<BR>for a 4oz tube and $30.99 for a 40oz can.<BR>That's not that bad considering that it lasts<BR>for a long time.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||14
Z||000012||FieroJoe||07-17-2001||10:45 PM||||My favorite interior dressing is Meguiar's Mirror Glaze #40.  It mildly cleans and then protects rubber, plastic, and vinyl.  This is thier professional line stuff, found in the tan bottles at most body shops, or Carquest, that's where I get my M/G stuff.  Makes the car smell like new car too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||West Coast Fiero||07-17-2001||11:17 PM||||From my experience, also other may know as well - stay away from Armor-All products as they are alcohol based and continued use of the product WILL rot, crack, and dry out what ever you apply it to. It was developed long before Synthetic based products like Formula 2001 ( which I could swear by ) which is why it is still sold, simply because of how long it has been around<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
